maria.chen: Quick heads-up: we've been getting mixed signals from SDKs and API responses about what to retry and what to show users. Want to align on a minimal error shape and SDK exception surface.
kevin: Yes please. Common issues: people retry on 401/403, or swallow 429. Also some SDKs return raw strings, others return objects. We should have typed exceptions and a stable machine code.
ash_winchester: Strong +1. Minimal server payload I like: semantic error_code, http_status, retryable bool, optional retry_after_seconds, user_message, developer_message, and meta.request_id. Keep it simple for clients.
danielle: For UX, expose user_message in sample apps, but devs can log developer_message. We should avoid leaking internal traces in user_message.
kevin: Example payload (server):
```json
{
  "error_code": "auth.invalid_api_key",
  "http_status": 401,
  "retryable": false,
  "retry_after_seconds": null,
  "user_message": "Invalid API key. Please update your credentials.",
  "developer_message": "token expired at 2026-03-15T09:03:00Z (req: abc123)",
  "meta": { "request_id": "abc123", "region": "us-west-2" }
}
```
kevin: SDK behavior proposal:
- Throw typed exceptions that extend a base `RedwoodError`.
- Exceptions should have stable fields: `code` (string), `httpStatus` (number), `retryable` (bool), `retryAfterSeconds` (number|null), `meta` (map) and `userMessage`/`developerMessage`.
- SDKs should NOT auto-retry unless `retryable === true` and caller opts in or endpoint metadata marks the call idempotent.
maria.chen: TS example for constructor:```ts
class RedwoodError extends Error {
  code: string;
  httpStatus: number;
  retryable: boolean;
  retryAfterSeconds?: number | null;
  meta: Record<string, unknown> | null;
  userMessage?: string;
  developerMessage?: string;
  constructor(payload: any) {
    super(payload.developer_message ?? payload.user_message ?? 'Request failed');
    this.code = payload.error_code;
    this.httpStatus = payload.http_status;
    this.retryable = !!payload.retryable;
    this.retryAfterSeconds = payload.retry_after_seconds ?? null;
    this.meta = payload.meta ?? null;
    this.userMessage = payload.user_message;
    this.developerMessage = payload.developer_message;
  }
}
```
kevin: In Python we mirror with exception classes: `class Unauthorized(RedwoodError)` and include same attrs. Keep error.message for backward compat until next major.
danielle: Action items:
1) Maria drafts short RFC with payload, SDK examples, and migration notes (EOW).
2) Ash to add middleware to server to normalize legacy HTTP -> new payload and inject request_id into meta.
3) I'll update onboarding sample app to show how to surface `user_message` safely and how to catch `RateLimitedError` to show a retry hint.
4) Kevin to add SDK compatibility tests and typed exception unit tests.
deploy-bot: deploy-bot: CI: branch `error-schema-unify` pushed, tests queued -> https://ci.internal/9901 :robot_face:
kevin: One more thing: for 5xx we mark `retryable: true` but sample apps should only auto-retry on idempotent endpoints. We'll add endpoint metadata field `idempotent: true|false` in docs.
maria.chen: Also include migration guidance: map old string messages into `developer_message` and keep `error.message` = `user_message` until major. I'll include concrete code samples for both SDKs.
kevin: Great. Let's sync on RFC comments tomorrow. Thanks all. :thumbsup:
